From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] seabraid: a lost helper closes its card, not the engine

A helper process that exited, went mute or answered wrongly used to end the
engine: RemoteExperts::seabraid_helper_finish waited 30 s, returned false without
closing the card, and the serve loop returned 1 (503 and a restart).  A restarted
engine then waited 1800 s on a stale kLoaded channel, and the prompt path probed
the helper with kill(pid, 0), which a recycled pid answers.

Detection: the engine binds a PeerWatch (pidfd opened first, then the /proc
starttime compared; one thread, one atomic, no signal ever sent) to the identity
the helper wrote before kHelperUp (wire v10 helper_start).  seabraid_closed() folds
the watch in, so every reader (EngineHost::helper_alive, RungIO::closed, the
retier loop, the ladder) sees a loss with no second predicate.  Close codes: 3
helper exited, 4 layer deadline, 5 helper error or bad echo, 6 gone at start.

Behaviour: every seabraid wait goes through bl_wait (pred or lost).  seabraid_helper_finish
on a loss, the 30 s deadline, ok == 0, a bad shape or non-finite reply calls seabraid_lose: the card is
closed and finish returns true with rows_lost() set.  The two dispatch sites
(expert_pool_dispatch, expert_pool_dispatch_multi) then compute the rows the
helper owed on the CPU (redo_lost_rows_single / _multi; the pure plan, with the
MAXT split, is include/strata/core/lost_rows.hpp; the window's activation
quantisation is one function used by both).  copy_cached_blobs closes and returns
all misses; a loss seen on a stager thread is only recorded (bl_note_loss) because
only the engine thread may rewrite the held bitmaps.  seabraid_open waits (120 s)
for kNone, binds the watch, and opens a stale or recycled channel as a closed
card (code 6) with one WARN instead of refusing.  The two ::kill(pid, 0) probes
in remote_prefill.cpp become seabraid_closed().

Tests: seabraid_helper_loss_test (L1-L9: real forked helpers killed by
raise(SIGKILL), parent never signals), lost_rows_test (L10); the opt and prefill
fixtures call announce_identity and the opt test's bad-echo cases now expect a
loss (closed 5, rows returned) instead of an error.

Failure-first (the tests built against the pre-0019 engine sources with the
new-API lines removed by sed, one scenario per run, CPU only): L1 Alarm clock
at 20 s (finish waits 30 s and returns false), L2 segfault at 4 s, L3 Alarm
clock at 20 s, L4 Alarm clock at 10 s, L5 FAIL closed==6 and "pid reused", L6
Alarm clock at 30 s, L7 Alarm clock at 20 s, L8 timeout at 60 s, L9 Alarm clock
at 20 s; lost_rows_test does not compile (no lost_rows.hpp).  With 0019 all
pass.  Sabotage (each fails its test): SB1 no "|| lost" in bl_wait: L1, L6;
SB2 no starttime compare: L5; SB3 deadline returns false: L3; SB4
seabraid_closed() without the watch: L2; SB5 no MAXT split: lost_rows_test; SB6
stale start refuses: L4.
